PATCH 543: two MISSING dispatch targets in the type-0x02 steering chain, and five sub-methods that
read a WORD command as a 4-byte int through a host pointer.

Found by auditing the type-0x02 sub-method tables the way patch 542 audited the 9e2b table.  `902c`
(the type-0x02 per-frame update, patch 365) dispatches two CS=0 tables with DI live:

    9060: call *%cs:-0x6f60(%bx)     ; table1 @0x90a0, bx = byte[di+0x3d] & 0x1e
    906a: call *%cs:-0x6e59(%bx)     ; table2 @0x91a7, bx = byte[di+0x3e]

Dumping both from the image and checking every target against the port:

    table1: 917d a202 a631 aa37 a202 91a6 90c0 ab03 9160 a202 91a6 a904 a9a0 a202 a46e ab03   (all present)
    table2: 91b7 a376 a3a8 a3e2 a3ec 0000 a3f6 a432 ...

`a3f6` (entry +12) and `a432` (entry +14) were NOT DEFINED IN THE PORT AT ALL -- the board:0015 class.
Both are real functions with the same shape:

    a3f6: push %cs ; call 0xaae8
          mov 0x90(%di),%bl ; xor %bh,%bh ; shl $1,%bx
          call *%cs:-0x5bf8(%bx)        ; CS=0 sub-table @0xa408 = {a410, a41b, a426, a427}
    a432: ... identical, sub-table @0xa444 = {a44c, a44c, a44c, a45c}

so those table entries dispatched into nothing and the steering command word[di+0x57] was never driven.

The six sub-targets all existed but were pristine, and every one of them carries TWO defects: the
object near offset is host-deref'd, and `word[di+0x57]` is a WORD (`cmpw`/`incw`/`decw`) that Ghidra
read and wrote as a 4-byte int -- which also clobbers the neighbouring field at [di+0x59].  The
compares are SIGNED (`jge`/`jle`).  Fixed here: a410, a41b, a427, a44c, a45c (a426 is a bare `ret` and
was already correct).  None of the six had any direct caller -- they are reachable only through the
tables the port could not dispatch -- so setting their convention to the near offset is free.

HONEST SCOPE: this does NOT make units move.  With it applied, AZER1/AZER4/SAUDI2 outcomes are
unchanged and the type-0x02 objects' positions are still frozen, with word[di+0x57] still 0.  It is
landed as what it is -- two missing functions and five width/base errors, all asm-verified -- and the
open question of whether type 0x02 is even supposed to translate is recorded in board:0020.

